;;; group-folded-into-world.slatl — Motoi Scheme Reference · broken-examples
;;;
;;; A broken-example is kept ON PURPOSE (CLAUDE.md § Broken-examples teach the
;;; differences). This one teaches a whole-LIBRARY rename: the `group/*`
;;; namespace (group/count, group/each, group/find) was never wired. The engine
;;; only ever had one entity collection — the world — and tag-scoped population
;;; queries live in the `world/*` library (chapter 72). So `group/*` was folded
;;; into `world/*` on 2026-07-25.
;;;
;;; Provenance for the DECISION: the running engine's names WIN over the
;;; reference for wrapper/alias verbs (authorized 2026-07-25). `world/count`,
;;; `world/each`, `world/find` are the wired names; `group/*` were a parallel
;;; naming surface that only existed on paper. The verbatim original 15-program
;;; chapter is archived at scratch/31-group.original.slat and its teaching value
;;; is captured below. Chapter 31 is now a redirect to chapter 72.
;;;
;;; IMPORTANT: the fold is NOT a pure textual swap — the world/* verbs have
;;; slightly different (better) return contracts than the group/* records
;;; claimed. Those differences are the real lesson.

(dialect :applies ("motoi") :note "broken-example — the group/* library folded into world/*")

(broken-example :name "group/count"
  :library "broken-examples"
  :teaches "library-fold-and-return-contract"
  :std-target "Motoi world/*"
  :std-rejected ("group/* (unwired alias namespace)")
  :status "folded"
  :training-eligible #t
  :provenance "scheme/reference/broken-examples/group-folded-into-world.slatl"

  ;; ─── THE BROKEN CODE (unbound symbol) ───
  :broken-code "(group/count 'enemy)"
  :broken-output "error: unbound symbol: group/count"
  :runs "no — group/count was never wired; the world is the only entity collection"

  ;; ─── WHY IT IS BROKEN ───
  :why
"Motoi has one entity collection — the world. There is no separate `group`
object to scope over, so a `group/` namespace never had anything to bind to.
Tag-scoped population queries are `world/count`, `world/each`, `world/find`
(chapter 72). The `group/*` spelling was a paper alias that duplicated the
world library under a second name — exactly the divergent-name duplication the
conformance ladder forbids. It was folded away, engine names winning."

  ;; ─── THE FIX ───
  :fix-code "(world/count 'enemy)"
  :fix-output "an integer — count of alive entities whose kind or tag is 'enemy"
  :fix-runs "yes"
  :fix-note
"Rename `group/count` → `world/count`. Identical contract: a pure, allocation-
free read returning a nonnegative integer. `(world/count)` with no tag counts
every alive entity."

  ;; ─── THE LESSON ───
  :lesson
"When two names describe one operation over one collection, Motoi keeps the
engine's wired name and drops the alias. `group/*` → `world/*`. But port by
reading the target's REAL contract, not by assuming the alias's docs were right:
  · group/each was documented to RETURN a count and pass an ID; world/each
    returns #<undefined> and passes the entity HANDLE. To count calls, close
    over a counter and compare to (world/count tag).
  · group/find was documented to return a list of IDs; world/find returns a
    list of entity HANDLES (and also accepts a predicate: (world/find pred)).
    (length (world/find tag)) still equals (world/count tag); (car (world/find
    tag)) yields a handle that every entity/* verb accepts directly."

  ;; ─── THE SAME IDEA IN THREE OTHER LIBRARIES ───
  :three-other-libs (
    (:lib "Motoi world/*"
     :status "the wired target — one collection, tag-scoped queries"
     :code "(world/count 'enemy)   (world/each 'enemy proc)   (world/find 'enemy)"
     :note "world/find also takes a predicate; world/each passes handles, returns undefined.")
    (:lib "Unity (C#)"
     :status "GameObject.FindGameObjectsWithTag returns an array of objects"
     :code "GameObject.FindGameObjectsWithTag(\"enemy\").Length"
     :note "Like world/find: you get object handles, not integer IDs. Count = array length.")
    (:lib "DOM / querySelectorAll"
     :status "returns a live-ish NodeList of element handles"
     :code "document.querySelectorAll('.enemy').length"
     :note "Same shape as world/find: handles you operate on, and .length is the count.")
  )

  :motoi-standard
"Target: `world/count` / `world/each` / `world/find` (chapter 72) as the single
tag-scoped population surface. The `group/*` alias namespace dropped from the
reference 2026-07-25; original 15-program chapter archived at
scratch/31-group.original.slat. Chapter 31 is now a redirect to chapter 72.")
